      "text": "Let $a = \\frac{x}{y}$, which is positive.\n\\[\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2} = \\frac{x^2 + 2xy + y^2}{x^2 + y^2} = 1 + \\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2}.\\]\nBy the AM-GM inequality, $\\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} < \\frac{2xy}{\\frac{x^2 + y^2}{2}} = \\frac{2xy \\sqrt{2}}{x^2 + y^2}.$\nAlso, by the AM-GM inequality, $\\frac{2xy \\sqrt{2}}{x^2 + y^2} < \\frac{2xy \\sqrt{2}}{(\\frac{x+y}{2})^2} = \\frac{4xy \\sqrt{2}}{x^2 + y^2}.$\nHence,\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2} &< 1 + \\frac{2xy \\sqrt{2}}{x^2 + y^2} \\\\\n&< 1 + \\frac{2xy \\sqrt{2} \\sqrt{2}}{x^2 + y^2} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{4xy}{x^2 + y^2} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{4xy}{(\\frac{x+y}{2})^2} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{16xy^2}{(x+y)^2} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{16xy^2}{\\frac{x^2 + 2xy + y^2}{2}} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{32xy^2}{x^2 + 2xy + y^2} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{1}{\\frac{x^2 + 2xy + y^2}{32xy^2}} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x^2 + y^2}{32xy^2} + 1\\right)^2}.\n\\end{align*}\nThus,\n\\[\\boxed{2}.\\] The answer is: 2",
